This is a parallel port on Alphas.  Use 9 or 7.  You have more interrupt
lines anyway.  SCSI controller can be normally found around 19.

> i think that the keyboard is on
> something like IRQ 1...?

Correct.

> maybe DMA addresses are messing it up??

Maybe.

> i hate dealing with problems like this!! :)

You are not the only one. :-)  Try first without any sound support at
all.  With 'make -j 5' it should not take very long to recompile
a kernel.

FYI - here is various info from two different working Alphas (parallel
port is not used on any of these).

$ cat /proc/interrupts 
 1:    86201   keyboard
 5:      164   sound blaster
12:  1396418   PS/2 Mouse
17:  5905099   DE500-AA (eth0)
19:  1227459   aic7xxx
$ cat /proc/ioports 
0060-006f : keyboard
0220-022f : sound blaster
